;; Where Chez Scheme 10.3.0's R6RS mode reads past R6RS's grammar (SCS5 (b); doc/scheme/SCHEME-SURVEY.md, "As built: SCS5"):
;; repr/scheme's reader reads as Chez does (§2, SM1), so a probe whose text a rule below matches is judged by Chez's recorded
;; dump (the pack scheme-chez-dumps), not by the report's grammar (arbace.repr.scheme.report), which calls it a violation.
;; A rule names its probes (:ids, test/scheme/probes.edn's ids) and the shape of their texts (:match, a regex on the text: a
;; probe it matches outside :ids reads the same both ways, e.g. an error in both). bin/repr-scheme report-check fails on a named
;; probe where the report and Chez agree (a stale rule) and on a probe outside the rules where they differ.
;; Found by bin/repr-scheme report-check (the report's reading of every probe against Chez's dump and Arbace's reader): these
;; three rules are every probe where the report and Chez differ: 37 probes at SCS5 (8, 7 and 22). Read with the Clojure reader.
[{:id :naninf-case
  :match #"[+-](?!inf\.0|nan\.0)(?i:inf\.0|nan\.0)"
  :ids ["num-0033" "num-0173" "num-0243" "num-0313" "num-0383" "num-0453" "num-0663" "num-0733"]
  :why "R6RS 4.2.1's <naninf> is nan.0 | inf.0, in lower case (the grammar spells the cases it allows elsewhere: #B, #E, #T, E, S, F, D, L, A-F); Chez reads +INF.0 as +inf.0"}
 {:id :radix-mantissa-width
  :match #"(?i)^(#[eixbod])*#[xbo](#[eixbod])*[0-9a-f]+\|[0-9]+$"
  :ids ["num-0235" "num-0305" "num-0375" "num-0515" "num-0585" "num-0655" "num-0725"]
  :why "R6RS 4.2.1's <mantissa width> follows a <decimal R>, which only radix 10 has (<decimal 10>); Chez takes #x1|53 as 1.0"}
 {:id :hash-after-prefixed-number
  :match #"(?i)^(#[eixbod])+[0-9a-f]+#"
  :ids ["num-0138" "num-0139" "num-0208" "num-0209" "num-0278" "num-0279" "num-0348" "num-0349" "num-0418" "num-0419" "num-0488" "num-0489" "num-0558" "num-0559" "num-0628" "num-0629" "num-0698" "num-0699" "num-0768" "num-0769" "num-0838" "num-0839"]
  :why "# is a <delimiter> (R6RS 4.2.1): #e1# is the number #e1 and then a # lexeme; Chez's reader keeps the R5RS digit placeholder # inside a prefixed number's token (number.ae's lenient-real?), and refuses the whole token"}]
